        "sv3-serums-calf-occurrence-audit"
      ],
      "primary_reading": "JCM1303 adds5ml heat-inactivated bovine calf serum among filter-sterilized additions. The actual existing Bovine_Calf_Serum import source is MD2061. Eight historical generic-label records plus one later Gibco label are reconstructed from the complete tracked recipe tree at15a4da5c08; historical generated TSV is not tracked. Eleven current local rows, including two later KOMODO rows, are separately captured. CCAP maps to gamma-irradiated fetal10109-155; DSM78d permits fetal/newborn; M2240 raw supplier name lacks product/heat bridge. DSM1245 PDF says inactivated calf, while its derived MediaDive row says fetal; that discrepancy is preserved as a boundary, not resolved by arbitrary preference.",
      "correction": "Retire sv1-kg-calf-serum1303 from active selection with no replacement payload, preserve all original source and proposal history, and leave the maintained owner untouched. Known preparation facts remain available in case158; no absent heat schedule or ontology blocks named partial representation.",
      "selection": "Precise source-continuity/occurrence partition hold, not a silently installable duplicate.",
      "options": [
        "Preserve the broad existing owner and attach occurrence-specific heat/filter facts without claiming separate ingredient identity; requires a supported occurrence/annotation representation and binding review.",
        "After an explicit source/occurrence partition, reconcile the authentic MD2061 lineage through the existing owner, preserving every broader/Gibco history/alias and routing excluded occurrences separately.",
        "If a curator establishes distinct material identities, prepare a separately reviewed split with complete history/occurrence bridges; do not treat missing metadata as proof."
      ],
      "prerequisites": [
        "Which fetal/newborn choice applies to each DSM78d occurrence.",
        "Gibco product/catalog/protocol and source applicability for M2240; no arbitrary mapping from its derived GMO label.",
        "Reviewed owner boundary and exact routing of JCM1303, CCAP, DSM78d, Gibco and later KOMODO occurrences; existing eight-count is historical, not an authorization to discard later/source-specific uses."
      ]
    },
    {
      "finding": "BIO-F04",
